  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+B(0){e}^{0}-2{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0 & =A-2 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}+B{e}^{x}-4{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =A{e}^{0}+B(0){e}^{0}+B{e}^{0}-4{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0 & =A+B-4 \\\\ 0 & =2+B-4 \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=2$ and $B=2,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}-2{e}^{2x}\n$$",
